[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m A regular octagon can be divided into 8 isosceles triangles by drawing lines from the center to each vertex. The central angle of each of these triangles is \( \frac{360^\circ}{8} = 45^\circ \). The side length of the octagon is given as 2.
