[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m assistant
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m [response] Let the three consecutive integers be \(n-1\), \(n\), and \(n+1\). The product of these integers is given by:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m (n-1)n(n+1) = 120
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m The mean of the three integers is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m \frac{(n-1) + n + (n+1)}{3} = \frac{3n}{3} = n
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m According to the problem, the product of the three integers divided by their mean is 24:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m \frac{(n-1)n(n+1)}{n} = 24
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m This simplifies to:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m (n-1)(n+1) = 24
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m This can be rewritten as:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m n^2 - 1 = 24
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m Solving for \(n\), we get:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m n^2 = 25 \implies n = 5 \text{ or } n = -5
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m We need to check both cases. If \(n = 5\), the three consecutive integers are 4, 5, and 6. Their product is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m 4 \times 5 \times 6 = 120
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m And the mean is 5, so:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m \frac{120}{5} = 24
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m This satisfies the conditions of the problem. If \(n = -5\), the three consecutive integers are -6, -5, and -4. Their product is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m -6 \times -5 \times -4 = -120
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m This does not satisfy the condition that the product is 120. Therefore, the only valid solution is \(n = 5\), and the largest of the three consecutive integers is:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m \boxed{6}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m [ground_truth] 6
