[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m [response] To solve the equation $x = \sqrt{11-2x} + 4$, we first isolate the square root term:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m \[x - 4 = \sqrt{11-2x}.\]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m Next, we square both sides to eliminate the square root:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m \[(x - 4)^2 = 11 - 2x.\]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m Expanding the left side, we get:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m \[x^2 - 8x + 16 = 11 - 2x.\]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m Rearranging all terms to one side of the equation, we have:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m \[x^2 - 8x + 2x + 16 - 11 = 0,\]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m \[x^2 - 6x + 5 = 0.\]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m This is a quadratic equation, which we can factor as:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m \[(x - 1)(x - 5) = 0.\]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m So, the solutions are:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m \[x = 1 \quad \text{or} \quad x = 5.\]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m 
