[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m \[ 8 \times 112 = m \times n, \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m which simplifies to:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m \[ m \times n = 896. \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m Since the gcd of $m$ and $n$ is 8, we can express $m$ and $n$ as $m = 8a$ and $n = 8b$, where $a$ and $b$ are coprime (i.e., $\text{gcd}(a, b) = 1$). Substituting these into the equation $m \times n = 896$, we get:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m \[ (8a) \times (8b) = 896, \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m which simplifies to:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m \[ 64ab = 896, \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m and further simplifies to:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m \[ ab = 14. \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m 
