[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m assistant
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m [response] To find out how many crab pots have three different colored balloons attached, we need to determine how many pots are marked with a red, blue, and yellow balloon simultaneously. This means we need to find the number of pots that are multiples of 4, 6, and 10 at the same time. The least common multiple (LCM) of 4, 6, and 10 will give us the interval at which a pot is marked with all three colors.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m First, we find the LCM of 4, 6, and 10. The prime factorizations are:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m - \(4 = 2^2\)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m - \(6 = 2 \times 3\)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m - \(10 = 2 \times 5\)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m The LCM is found by taking the highest power of each prime that appears in the factorizations:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m - The highest power of 2 is \(2^2\)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m - The highest power of 3 is \(3\)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m - The highest power of 5 is \(5\)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m 
