[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m The key is to recognize that the point $E$ must be symmetrically opposite to $D$ with respect to the plane that contains $A, B, C$. The centroid of the triangle $ABC$ is the point that is equidistant from $A, B, C$, and it can be calculated as the average of the coordinates of $A, B, C$:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m \[G = \left(\frac{-1+1+1}{3}, \frac{1-1+1}{3}, \frac{1+1-1}{3}\right) = \left(\frac{1}{3}, \frac{1}{3}, \frac{1}{3}\right).\]
