[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m [response] To find $h^{-1}(5)$, we first need to find the inverse function $h^{-1}(y)$ of $h(y) = \dfrac{1+y}{2-y}$. We start by setting $h(y) = x$ and solving for $y$ in terms of $x$.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m Given $x = \dfrac{1+y}{2-y}$, we can rearrange this equation to solve for $y$:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m \[x(2-y) = 1+y\]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m \[2x - xy = 1 + y\]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m \[2x - 1 = y + xy\]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m \[2x - 1 = y(1 + x)\]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m 
