[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m [response] Given the polynomial $p(x) = x^2 + ax + b$ with roots $2a$ and $b$, we can use Vieta's formulas which relate the coefficients of the polynomial to sums and products of its roots. According to Vieta's formulas, for a quadratic equation $x^2 + px + q = 0$ with roots $r_1$ and $r_2$, we have $r_1 + r_2 = -p$ and $r_1r_2 = q$.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m Applying Vieta's formulas to our polynomial $p(x) = x^2 + ax + b$ with roots $2a$ and $b$, we get:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m 1. $2a + b = -a$ (sum of the roots)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m 2. $2ab = b$ (product of the roots)
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m From the first equation, we can solve for $b$:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m \[2a + b = -a \implies b = -3a\]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m From the second equation, we can solve for $a$ and $b$:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m \[2ab = b \implies b(2a - 1) = 0\]
