[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m Notice that $z^{23} = 1$, so $z^{2n} = z^{2n \mod 23}$. The key insight is to recognize that the terms in the sum are symmetric and can be paired up. Specifically, for each $n$, there exists an $m$ such that $z^n + z^{2n} = z^m + z^{2m}$ due to the cyclic nature of the roots of unity.
