[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m The second inequality $f(x) - f(y) \le 0$ simplifies to $(x+3)^2 - (y+3)^2 \le 0$, which can be factored as $((x+3) - (y+3))((x+3) + (y+3)) \le 0$ or $(x-y)(x+y+6) \le 0$. This inequality describes the region between the lines $y = x$ and $y = -x - 6$.
