[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m The first condition $f(x) + f(y) \le 0$ implies that the sum of the values of the function at $x$ and $y$ must be less than or equal to zero. Since the minimum value of $f(x)$ is $-8$, both $f(x)$ and $f(y)$ must be in the range $[-8, 0]$ for their sum to be less than or equal to zero.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m 
