[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m assistant
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m [response] To find the center of the sphere given by the equation
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m \[x^2 + 4x + y^2 - 10y + z^2 + 2z + 5 = 0,\]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m we need to complete the square for each variable.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m For \(x\), we have \(x^2 + 4x\), which can be written as \((x + 2)^2 - 4\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m For \(y\), we have \(y^2 - 10y\), which can be written as \((y - 5)^2 - 25\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m For \(z\), we have \(z^2 + 2z\), which can be written as \((z + 1)^2 - 1\).
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m Substituting these into the original equation, we get
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m \[(x + 2)^2 - 4 + (y - 5)^2 - 25 + (z + 1)^2 - 1 + 5 = 0.\]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m Simplifying, we have
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m \[(x + 2)^2 + (y - 5)^2 + (z + 1)^2 - 25 = 0,\]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m or
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m \[(x + 2)^2 + (y - 5)^2 + (z + 1)^2 = 25.\]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m This is the standard form of a sphere with center \((-2, 5, -1)\) and radius \(5\). Therefore, the center of the sphere is \(\boxed{(-2, 5, -1)}\).
