[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m Since the GCD of $m$ and $n$ is 8, we can express $m$ and $n$ as $m = 8a$ and $n = 8b$, where $a$ and $b$ are coprime (i.e., $\text{GCD}(a, b) = 1$). Substituting these into the equation $m \times n = 896$, we get $8a \times 8b = 896$, which simplifies to $ab = 14$. The pairs $(a, b)$ that satisfy this equation and are coprime are $(1, 14)$ and $(2, 7)$.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m For the pair $(1, 14)$, we have $m = 8 \times 1 = 8$ and $n = 8 \times 14 = 112$, so $m + n = 120$.
