[36m(TaskRunner pid=2059637)[0m [response] The dot product of two vectors $\mathbf{v}$ and $\mathbf{w}$ is given by $\mathbf{v} \cdot \mathbf{w} = \|\mathbf{v}\|\|\mathbf{w}\|\cos\theta$, where $\theta$ is the angle between the vectors. Given $\|\mathbf{v}\| = 3$ and $\|\mathbf{w}\| = 4$, we have $\mathbf{v} \cdot \mathbf{w} = 12\cos\theta$. The minimum value of $\cos\theta$ is $-1$, which occurs when $\theta = 180^\circ$. Therefore, the minimum value of $\mathbf{v} \cdot \mathbf{w}$ is $12 \times -1 = -12$. Thus, the answer is $\boxed{-12}$.
